# A bare name that is both a type of the program and an associated type of a trait in
# scope is the program's own type (ruling AQ): an impl's equation `type Reason Player =
# Reason` names no associated type of `^Document`, and `Reason Board Player` gives the
# program's `Reason`, which takes no parameter, two; each is refused with the associated
# type written through its trait, `^Document.Reason`, as its fix. Written by Claude (round after q11), 16 November 2026;
# subject to change.
trait ^Document d:
    type Role
    type Reason (r: Role d)

type GameRole = choice:
    Player
    Spectator
derive ^Eq, ^Ord

type Reason = choice:
    NotYourMove
derive ^Eq

type Board = choice:
    Board

impl ^Document Board:
    type Role = GameRole
    type Reason Player = Reason
    type Reason Spectator = Never

Why: fn Reason Board Player -> Text
fn Why NotYourMove = "not your move"
